## DC 1 — Company and Services

Normain AB (Sweden) provides an AI-powered automation platform that ingests customer content from connected file storage (SharePoint, Google Drive, Box), direct uploads in the platform UI, and customer-supplied URLs, processes it with AI models hosted in Microsoft Azure, and produces insights and structured outputs.

**Hosting modes offered.** All four modes below are actively offered. Normain recommends Logical separation as the default; Physical separation is offered to customers with heightened data-isolation requirements; Customer-hosted is available but Normain advises against it.

| Mode | Description |
|---|---|
| **SaaS — Open platform (Normain-managed)** | Customer organisation provisioned within Normain's multi-organisation platform tenant at `app.normain.com`, on Normain's shared Microsoft Azure environment. |
| **Logical separation (Normain-managed)** | Customer receives a dedicated subdomain, Kubernetes namespace, PostgreSQL database, storage container, NFS share, and Entra ID integration. All resources run within Normain's shared Microsoft Azure environment (shared AKS cluster, PostgreSQL server, Key Vault, Container Registry, and AI services). |
| **Physical separation (Normain-managed)** | Customer receives a dedicated Azure resource group operated by Normain, with dedicated AKS cluster, PostgreSQL server, Key Vault, storage accounts, and supporting Azure resources provisioned exclusively for the customer. |
| **Customer-hosted (Microsoft Azure)** | Same architecture as Physical separation, deployed in a Microsoft Azure tenant provided and operated by the Customer using Normain-published Terraform modules. Available but not recommended by Normain. |

During the examination period, customers operate under the SaaS Open-platform and Logical separation modes. Customer-hosted has no customers until after the period end (4 August 2026) and is not in scope for this examination. Physical separation has no customers as of the draft cut-off date; should a customer onboard onto Physical separation before 4 August 2026, this section and DC 3 will be updated at issuance. Physical separation reuses the same Terraform modules and the same change-management, vulnerability-scanning, and monitoring controls described in DC 5, applied to a dedicated Azure resource group.

**Customer input integrations**: SharePoint, Google Drive, Box (read-only, via OAuth or Microsoft Graph), plus direct UI upload and customer-supplied URL ingestion.

