## DC 2 — Principal Service Commitments and System Requirements

**Availability (Service Level Agreement).** The SLA (Attachment 2 to the Main Agreement; latest version 2025-12-17) commits to:

| Commitment | Value |
|---|---|
| Platform uptime | ≥ 99 % per calendar month |
| Service credit — uptime 90.0 % – 98.9 % | 5 % of monthly fee |
| Service credit — uptime < 90 % | 10 % of monthly fee |
| Planned interruptions | Max 2 per month, ≤ 4 hours each |
| Service window | Swedish non-holiday weekdays, 08:00 – 22:00 UTC+2 |
| Claim window | 5 business days from end of affected month |

Service credits do not apply to outages caused by force majeure, customer-attributable issues, or emergency maintenance (full exclusions in the SLA). Availability is not within the scope of this examination (see DC 8).

**Regulatory and contractual commitments**

- GDPR Article 32 technical and organizational measures.
- Support for customer DPIAs.
- Personal-data breach notification per DPA.
- Subprocessor change notification: at least 14 days' prior notice, with the customer's right to terminate the affected subscription if it does not approve (Microsoft Commercial Marketplace Standard Contract §2.3.d).
- Data return or erasure on contract termination per DPA.
- Data-security commitments (per customer Order; e.g. Marketplace Order §5): logical tenant isolation, no standing employee access to customer databases (Azure PIM-gated and time-limited), immutable audit logging retained at least 365 days, encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest, and EU-only data residency.

System requirements (internal): adherence to the Information Security Policy, change-management process, and access-management policy approved by the ISMS Governance Council.

