## DC 6 — Complementary User Entity Controls (CUECs)

User entities (customers) are expected to operate the following controls to complement the controls described above. Failure to operate any of these may impair the platform's ability to meet its commitments.

| TSC | CUEC |
|---|---|
| CC1.4 | The customer is responsible for performing background or pre-employment screening of its own users granted access to the platform, where legally permitted. |
| CC2.1 | The customer is responsible for the appropriate classification and protection of data submitted to the platform. |
| CC2.3 | The customer is responsible for the accuracy, completeness, and authorization of inputs and instructions submitted to the platform by its users. |
| CC6.1 | The customer is responsible for defining roles, entitlements, and authorization rules for its own users within the platform. |
| CC6.2 | The customer is responsible for issuing, storing, rotating, and revoking platform user credentials and API keys belonging to its users. |
| CC6.3 | The customer is responsible for periodically reviewing the access rights granted to its own users within the platform. |
| CC6.6 (a) | The customer is responsible for protecting data in transit between its own systems and the platform endpoints. |
| CC6.6 (b) | The customer is responsible for the physical and environmental security of end-user devices used to access the platform. |
| CC8.1 | The customer is responsible for configuring its own platform integrations (e.g., SharePoint, Google Drive, Box), including the scope of credentials issued and the data made accessible to the platform. |

