## DC 7 — Complementary Subservice Organization Controls (CSOCs)

The system uses two carved-out subservice organizations for the production data path: Microsoft Azure (all modes) and Amazon Web Services (AWS), which hosts Anthropic models in the SaaS open-platform mode. Other named third parties listed in DC 3.5 receive non-database telemetry (BetterStack) or product-analytics events (PostHog) and are not relied on for the trust services criteria below.

Azure OpenAI Service, Azure Document Intelligence, Azure Speech Service, and Azure Communication Services are operated by Microsoft as part of the Azure subservice and are covered by the Microsoft Azure SOC 2 Type 2 report. The Anthropic models used in SaaS mode are hosted on AWS and covered by the AWS SOC 2 Type 2 report.

| TSC | CSOC expected of Microsoft Azure and AWS |
|---|---|
| CC6.4 | Physical access controls at Azure and AWS data centers. |
| CC7.2 | Environmental controls — fire suppression, power redundancy, temperature, humidity — at Azure and AWS data centers. |

Management receives and reviews the Microsoft Azure SOC 2 Type 2 report (via the Microsoft Service Trust Portal) and the AWS SOC 2 Type 2 report at least annually.

